{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md'","aggregated_output":"SEMANTIC REVIEW Use the supplied contract against fixed inputs, source dependencies and observations. One checker_correspondence review covers requirement versus encoded predicate, entry/caller duties, oracle, identity, legal history, observation path/completion and counterevidence. Use experiments.md for these criteria, including wait/cleanup ownership and finite progress observations; unexamined continuation triggers remain gaps under the stated scheduling assumptions. Applicability and decomposition need separate answers only for concrete issues. No issue found is provisional, not proof or an independent vote.\n\nCURRENT VERSION Cite unchanged established parts and focus on the increment: what changed, which premise it answers, what the new execution observed and what remains unanswered. Verify that the fixed entry, prefix and schedule still exercise the original discriminator: stronger setup must not exclude the investigated premise. A narrower scope cannot settle its parent; substantive changes use the existing revision rules. New inputs require fresh execution and correspondence; old review success cannot certify them. Scope/cause/consequence questions outside the checked proposition are independent limits, not additional confirmation gates. Never alter a requirement or weaken a predicate merely to obtain a passing test.\n\nISSUES Fixed Claim, Harness and Monitor conflicts have exact issue/condition records. Address the listed issue with a sourced resolution and, where supplied, condition dispositions; do not answer the same conflict separately in several products. A no_issue_found item alone clears nothing. Preserve current counterevidence as an open issue, explained alternatives in rationale and independent limits in limitations. Resolution applies to its answering version and descendants; it does not legalize an older driver. Shared semantic issues follow actual dependencies, not checker names.\n\nREPAIR Distinguish review aspect from challenged component. F4 repairs unreached experiment prerequisites. Ordinary technical repair preserves shared property descriptions, events, identities, predicates and legality; it needs no preliminary review or encoding refactor unless an actual dispute/change requires one. Tool, parser and framework failures are not semantic feedback. Executed harness changes require a new artifact, fresh execution and current correspondence. Driver/configuration/initialization repairs name repair_issue_ids, preserve the requirement and oracle, and replace only sourced current premises. Changed observation/oracle encoding uses explicit correction; changed normative meaning/applicability uses F2, and proposition-preserving dependency expansion uses F3. Resolve against the actual changed component, never an unrelated edit. If additional source evidence answers the issue without changing inputs, resolve on that executed version instead of manufacturing a harness rewrite. Remaining issues and the current version's missing correspondence stay visible independently.\n# Investigation and selection\n\nCandidate investigates a sourced question, including unknown requirements, protection premises or legal history. Obligation fixes an applicable responsibility without presuming violation; Check supplies inputs, history and observations. Missing authority calls for contract investigation, missing history for source work or conditional exploration. Neither gap bars a Candidate or licenses an invented obligation.\n\nFirst explain both core relationships from activity_roles and their connection in AuditSpec.core_overview. Follow representative work through owners, qualified support, aggregation, decision, propagation and consumption; explain acquisition, change and loss of context/authority and handling of old requests, replies, pending support and established decisions. Read the supporting membership, history, recovery and completion mechanisms needed for this backbone. Trace callers and callees, important rejection, retry and asynchronous paths; deeper variants may remain open.\n\nSave early discrepancies as sourced Surfaces or specific unknowns even when no obligation is ready. Distinguish open_details from core_gaps: unexplained formation, authority transition or old-work handling breaks readiness; a usable overview can retain local anomalies. Only a preconfigured directed_question permits a proportionate local boundary first; activity_focus does not. A usable map and first Candidate may share a product. Unmapped source work and exploration need no fabricated Fact.\n\nUse behavior-facts.md for implementation meaning. Select a principal Fact lifecycle with a sourced A1/A2 connection; a question need not span both. Direct behavior_ids establish, consume, invalidate or reinterpret it; supporting_behavior_ids explain separate history/context/consequence support. Cross-activity effects establish actual relationships without relabeling support Activities. Names and protocol labels establish neither relevance nor responsibility.\n\nUse question, counterevidence, unknowns, importance and trigger_rationale to identify what remains unexplained, what existing protection does establish, and what the next action will distinguish. A concise sourced difference suffices; no ranking, mandatory alternative list or confidence threshold. Compare contract reading, smaller exploration and another known relationship before committing to a costly test. “This input has not been run” alone is not a discriminator. An empty unknowns list does not disqualify a check whose earlier investigation established its value.\n\nWhen sourced mechanisms answer the specific suspicion, submit explained and reselect. An unconstructed single obligation may remain unexecuted; this is neither holds nor a budget refund. Fixed artifacts, directed execution tasks, changed premises and open disputes remain visible until explicitly handled. An explicit guard with unresolved ownership, timing, producer or context instead calls for investigation of that premise. A negative result should identify the plausible explanation it excluded and independent premises left open; distinguish it from execution corroborating an already-explained protection. Neither settles the entire Fact or becomes a reason to expand input variants indefinitely. Keep one requirement's independent scenarios together; a genuinely different responsibility gets its own question.\n\nConditional differences with unclear contracts remain exploration or local pause. Once responsibility is grounded, obligation and construction may be separate products. Reuse helpers and legal prefixes only after checking their entry, caller duties, completion order and fault assumptions for this question. A convenient driver must not exclude permitted overlap that supplied the discriminator, nor assume a looser ordering is legal because it produces a difference. Fixed checks must still exercise the investigated premise; a narrower child cannot settle its parent. Use existing F2/F3 when requirement or scope changes. Finish necessary technical repair and review of accepted work; switching questions preserves its debt.\n\nPrioritize consensus safety and explicitly scoped progress duties. Distinguish a sourced numeric/event deadline, implementation-owned automatic continuation without a numeric deadline, and later work explicitly owed by the caller. No numeric deadline does not preclude investigating lost continuation triggers; the word automatic alone supplies no obligation. A possible later event in a comment is not a guarantee that callers produce it. Independently grounded eligibility, accounting, wakeup or correlation duties can be resolved without a client endpoint or global consequence. Shared facts and helpers transfer understanding, not results.\n\nAt natural handoffs retain the answered proposition and remaining discriminator in feedback using tasks/audit.md references. In the next already-needed related map submission, replace the answered original unknown with its sourced conditional relationship and remove obsolete progress reminders. Correct materially misleading higher-level summaries in that same product before reuse; harmless wording differences need no cleanup turn or whole-map sweep. Preserve independent unknowns and historical inputs. Consult the actual answer and assessment, not an understanding label or reference alone. Use behavior-facts.md for primary ownership instead of copying one answer across layers. Source work and exploration may continue from feedback; near expiry save minimal complete learning.\n\nOpen runs continue investigation until controller time/call or actual interruption boundaries. Empty pending_work or disposed registered questions does not exhaust the frontier: use the overview, other consumers/contexts, Surfaces and unread paths. Unit admission exhaustion still permits sourced Candidates, premise investigation and authorized exploration without immediate escalation. Follow each capacity separately; do not repeat handoffs, rerun explained guards, reuse an old Claim for a new proposition or refill budgets. Take a smaller informative step near expiry. Only a preconfigured finite directed task may complete early. Actual cancellation, safety refusal, permission loss and unrecoverable service/tool failure still stop.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The repaired run reached the intended delta transfer. Before dispatch, the follower held `{11:110}` and the leader held all three keys. After synchronization, the follower reported decided, accepted and compacted indexes of 3, but returned only `{22:220,33:330}`. The raw trace shows the missing key had already been decided and received; I found no correspondence issue for this scoped content-preservation check.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nsid=['s_snapshot_doc','s_storage_contract','s_sync_test_expectation','s_sync','s_memory','s_read','s_follower','s_pending','s_leader_sync','s_api','s_network_doc','s_leader_decision']\nrationale='''The fixed v2 artifact preserves the v1 requirement, schedule, event identities and comparison; only the unavailable optional logger initializer was removed. I inspected the fixed harness and plan and the actual run 4c1e4585ab8748119316ce21b39868e9. The snapshot documentation requires preservation of application state rather than data-discarding trim, and its key/value create/overwrite-merge example is matched by this BTreeMap implementation. The Snapshot trait and sync-test expectation independently identify delta reconstruction as recovery of decided state. The oracle compares actual canonical application contents, not index equality or Rust test success.\n\nConstruction uses three default MemoryStorage instances, validated configuration [1,2,3], public try_become_leader, append, outgoing-message extraction, incoming dispatch and reconnected calls. No protocol message or storage state is fabricated. Transport ordinals 1-20 establish the prepare/accept history; ordinals 21-26 replicate and decide key 11 at all replicas. The common_prefix event and precondition assertions establish that node 3 actually exposes that key at decided index 1. During disconnection, only traffic to/from node 3 is dropped; nodes 1 and 2 decide keys 22 and 33 through their real acknowledgments. Restored endpoint callbacks produce PrepareReq at 37-38, Prepare at 39, Promise at 40 reporting accepted=decided=1, and actual AcceptSync at 41 carrying Delta({22:220,33:330}), sync index 3, decided index 3, same configuration/ballot and new session 2. Per-producer queue order is preserved. There are no injected timer requirements or numeric liveness claims; this finite public-API history can occur between ticks. The handler's ballot and Prepare-phase guards are satisfied by actual preparation, not only a role label.\n\nAdmission and result at ordinal 41 share independent case/node/ordinal identity. Admission precedes dispatch, records old state {11:110}, and captures leader state {11:110,22:220,33:330}, with the leader state independently corroborated by node 2 before restoration. The result follows synchronous handle_incoming return under exclusive Rust ownership, records phase Accept and decided=accepted=compacted=3, and reads actual stored snapshot content through read_decided_suffix. It returns {22:220,33:330}. Ordinal 42 is the real Accepted reply at index 3; the final quiescent read retains the same content mismatch. There is exactly one matching admission/result and the retained monitor assessment has no parsing errors and a complete unequal comparison. Setup assertions concern preceding legal history and message shape; none require the principal content assertion to hold or select the scenario by outcome.\n\nThe source explains this witness: sync_log first replaces cached decided_idx with 3, then the Delta branch invokes create_decided_snapshot; create_snapshot requests storage entries [0,3) while the follower only stores [0,1). MemoryStorage returns an empty vector for the incomplete interval. Merging the transmitted delta therefore loses key 11 and the transaction stores the resulting snapshot at compacted index 3. This causal account follows current source and actual input/output, not an instrumented observation of private intermediates. Ballot/phase checks and atomic grouping establish admissibility and completion but do not repair the content. Complete-snapshot replacement is an alternative branch, not contrary evidence for this observed delta. The completed local counterexample needs no unobserved runtime/client endpoint or disk-crash claim.'''\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id='a5fd40b0afc54d27bef5dbc6bf7217df',rationale='Current fixed execution reaches the intended delta history and completes a content-preservation comparison; review the actual witness rather than test status.',review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=sid,rationale=rationale,counterevidence=['The run satisfies existing ballot, phase and recovery-session mechanisms; they do not establish snapshot content preservation.','The Complete snapshot branch has different base construction and is not exercised.'],limitations=['Observed one same-ballot reconnect with MemoryStorage and documented key/value semantics.','The private intermediate empty base is inferred from the source and actual transfer, not independently instrumented.','Disk atomicity, cross-configuration routing, runtime subscribers and broader propagation of corrupted snapshots are outside this observation.'],report_title='增量快照同步丢失已决定的键',report_answer='三节点合法断连重连后，跟随者的决定、接受和压缩索引均为 3，但读取状态从包含键 11 变成仅包含键 22、33；领导者仍包含全部三个键。固定执行完成了内容比较，作用域限于本次内存存储的同轮次增量同步。')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['4c1e4585ab8748119316ce21b39868e9','989cd3774fd64cc7a64dbf62dd088787','b_sync','b_read','f_snapshot','s_sync','s_memory'],answered='The actual legal reconnect reaches the questioned delta branch and loses an already decided key: the follower changes from {11:110} to {22:220,33:330}, while the leader retains all three keys. Decided/accepted/compacted indexes all become 3. The complete correlated content comparison is violated; this submission supplies current correspondence review, leaving final attribution to the controller.',remaining=['Continue separate frontier investigation: buffered StopSign lifecycle, runtime completion and configuration-routing ownership remain open.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The concrete prefix-boundary uncertainty is answered for the fixed MemoryStorage history. Do not rerun variants merely to corroborate this witness.',question_updates={'989cd3774fd64cc7a64dbf62dd088787':dict(unknowns=[],resume_conditions=[])}))\njson.dump(s,open('delta_review_submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['delta_review_submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(p.stdout);print(p.stderr)\nPY\npython3 make_review.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
